    "https://chatham.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/ChathamUniversity/job/Pittsburgh-PA/Director-of-Alumni-Engagement_JR00000962": {
      "title": "Director of Alumni Engagement",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-28\nFull time\n\nChatham University welcomes your interest in employment opportunities and encourages you to review open positions. Please note that Chatham does not accept unsolicited applications. Director of Alumni Engagement Chatham University seeks a creative, relationship-oriented, and execution-focused professional to serve as Director of Alumni Engagement . Reporting to the Senior Director of Advancement, this role is responsible for designing and delivering meaningful engagement experiences that strengthen relationships with alumni and donors and inspire philanthropic support. This is a hands-on leadership role for someone who enjoys both strategy and execution, developing engagement programs while actively managing events, communications, and volunteer initiatives. The Director will play a key role in building a vibrant, connected alumni community and enhancing the donor experience across the institution. The Director of Alumni Engagement oversees and directs all aspects of alumni programming that seek to engage alumni with the University and to develop relationships that encourage alumni to advance the university’s mission by volunteering, mentoring, attending events, and making financial contributions. The Director will play a vital role in developing distinct alumni engagement programs relevant for Chatham’s diverse alumni population: alumnae from its time as an undergraduate women’s college, graduates of its professional and graduate degree programs, and now alumni as an all-gender institution served on three campuses. Specifically, the Director of Alumni Engagement directs, manages, and administers all matters that enhance the university’s ability to weave alumni into the fabric of the University, from managing reunion programs and event planning to growing and overseeing volunteer engagement opportunities to encouraging alumni to become mentors to students and to financially support the university. The Director of Alumni Engagement will build effective relationships with departments including enrollment management, student affairs and career development, and marketing and communications to effectively engage alumni. Duties and Responsibilities: Develop programs consistent with the University’s strategic plan and ensure that programs effectively address objectives and priorities, operate within budget limitations, and comply with appropriate policies. Coordinate activities with fundraising staff in order to identify and cultivate major gift prospects and to build programming opportunities that encourage philanthropic support. Ensure that events are well executed, mission-driven, and aligned with engagement and fundraising goals. Establish and build relationships with alumni locally, regionally, and nationally; maintain regular communication with alumni via direct contact and the coordination of alumni communication programs such as e-mail, the website, and print communications. Develop and enhance geographic, academic, and affinity group alumni programs through the planning and implementation of events and other alumni gatherings and engagement. Conceptualize, plan, and coordinate alumni volunteer efforts in conjunction with other university departments. Qualifications: At least five years’ experience working in an effective, comprehensive alumni relations office. Experience managing diverse groups of volunteers, boards, and alumni networks. Strong project management and organizational skills. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Familiarity with advancement CRM’s, preferably Virtuous. Willingness to travel and work evenings and weekends. Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree preferred. Salary Range:  $55,000 - 60,000. 40-hour work week. Exact compensation based on candidate skills and experience.  How to Apply:  Applications accepted only via www.chatham.edu/careers  (direct link is https://chatham.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/ChathamUniversity/job/Pittsburgh-PA/Director-of-Alumni-Engagement_JR00000962 ) and follow the instructions to complete the application process. To ensure full consideration, please include:  Cover Letter outlining your qualifications for the position  Curriculum Vitae or Resume  Contact information for three professional references  All application materials should be uploaded at the same time at the time of application. The system will not allow applicants to make edits to their applications after submission. Chatham University strives to promote a campus environment that understands and embraces multiculturalism while increasing individuals' intercultural competence. We actively work to build and sustain a diverse and culturally vibrant campus, which promotes employee and student success and retention.   Chatham University is an Equal Opportunity Employer with a strong commitment to diversity, inclusion, and equity. Chatham University does not discriminate on the basis of race, creed, color, religion, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, age, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, marital or family status, political affiliation, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law."
    },
    "https://chatham.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/ChathamUniversity/job/Pittsburgh-PA/Adjunct-Instructor---Business_JR00000155": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Business",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-26\nPart time\n\nChatham University welcomes your interest in employment opportunities and encourages you to review open positions. Please note that Chatham does not accept unsolicited applications. Adjunct  Faculty       Do you want to share your professional knowledge and experience as an adjunct instructor? Chatham University is looking for talented adjunct instructors to teach undergraduate and graduate level courses at their three campuses ( Shadyside, Eastside , and Eden Hall ) and online.       Adjunct instructors must have at least a master's degree in a related field.   Please take a look at the full curriculum at www.chatham.edu/academics  to identify courses that match your expertise .       Interested candidates should visit  www.chatham.edu/careers  and follow the instructions to complete the application process.  Candidates should include in their cover letter their background and experience related to the discipline of interest . Prior teaching experience is a plus.  Chatham University offers a competitive adjunct salary.     Looking for adjuncts with expertise in various fields of business, including :    Accounting   Applied Data Science   Economics   International Business   Management   Marketing   Sustainability Management   Project Management       Chatham University is an Equal Opportunity Employer         Adjunct Business Faculty   Chatham University seeks to fill several Adjunct Instructor opportunities in the ir IACBE - accredited Department of Business and Entrepreneurship. I ndividuals with professional experience and training in the areas of management, accounting, economics, data science, business analytics, sustainability management, supply chain management, project management, marketing, and international business are encouraged to apply.     The Department of Business and Entre p reneurship infuse s its curriculum with the University’s core values of sustainability , community engagement, and inclusion. Instructors may utilize a variety of teaching methods to promote student engagement such as experiential learning, group d i scussion, project work , simulations, case analysis, field trips, guest lecture s , multimedia , or other techniqu es.     Chatham University strives to promote a campus environment that understands and embraces multiculturalism while increasing individuals' intercultural competence. We actively work to build a nd sustain a diverse and culturally vibrant campus, which promotes employee and student success and retention.   Review of applications is ongoing.    Position Summary:   Adjunct position s will be filled as needed in the fields of Business Management, Economics , International Business , Marketing , Accounting, Supply Chain Management , Innovation, Sustainability Management, Data Science and Business Analytics.    We welcome adjunct faculty who bring creativity , enthusiasm and a collaborat ive a pproach to their teaching and course development .   Primary Responsibilities:   Teaching undergraduate and graduate level courses in business disciplines .   Consulting and collaborating with other faculty to align course content with departmental teaching goals and objectives .    P articipati ng in university and department events, committees, meetings, and academic advising as needed.   Participating in adjunct instructor training sessions.   Required Qualifications:   Completion of a master’s degree in business or relevant field .     Preferred Qualifications:     Completion of a doctoral degree in business or relevant field.   Candidates with college teaching and mentoring experience.    Candidates with professional and/or lived experiences that advance the university’s commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion.   Chatham University strives to promote a campus environment that understands and embraces multiculturalism while increasing individuals' intercultural competence. We actively work to build and sustain a diverse and culturally vibrant campus, which promotes employee and student success and retention.   Chatham University is an Equal Opportunity Employer with a strong commitment to diversity, inclusion, and equity. Chatham University does not discriminate on the basis of race, creed, color, religion, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, age, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, marital or family status, political affiliation, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law."
    },
    "https://chatham.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/ChathamUniversity/job/Pittsburgh-PA/Senior-Director-of-Advancement-Services_JR00000961": {
      "title": "Senior Director of Advancement Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-25\nFull time\n\nChatham University welcomes your interest in employment opportunities and encourages you to review open positions. Please note that Chatham does not accept unsolicited applications. Senior Director of Advancement Services Chatham University seeks a collaborative, strategic, and focused professional to oversee the operations and infrastructure that facilitate and support the University’s fundraising and alumni engagement efforts.  Reporting to the Vice President for Advancement, the Senior Director of Advancement Services will lead an advancement services team responsible for gift processing, data management and reporting, prospect research and management, stewardship and donor relations, advancement communications, and strategic planning.  The Senior Director will play an important role in the Advancement Office’s evolution over the next several years, improving processes, enhancing reporting and analytics, and creating an integrated donor experience that enables philanthropic growth and long-term engagement. Duties and Responsibilities: Advancement Operations and Strategy:  Lead the day-to-day advancement services operations, ensuring effective systems, workflows, and processes that support Advancement unit goals.  Help create, refine, and execute strategic plans and objectives for the department.  Develop and implement best practices related to data integrity, gift processing, stewardship, donor communications, prospect research and management, and reporting.  Serve as a key resource and authority for Advancement staff on policies, procedures, and database management. Data Management and Gift Processing:  Oversee database management, including data entry standards, record maintenance, reporting, and data hygiene.  Ensure the accuracy and integrity of donor, alumni, and prospect information.  Oversee all gift processing activities, including gift entry, acknowledgements, reconciliation, and reporting in close coordination with business office partners.  Establish and maintain policies and procedures that ensure timely, accurate, and confidential handling of donor information and contributions.  Produce regular reports, dashboards, and analytics to support fundraising strategy, campaign tracking, and leadership decision making. Stewardship and Donor Relations:  Oversee acknowledgement processes, donor recognition, impact reporting, and stewardship communications.  Develop systems to ensure timely and meaningful engagement with donors.  Support donor recognition programs and stewardship initiatives. Advancement Communications:  Oversee Advancement-related communications in partnership with University colleagues and Advancement leadership.  Help develop and coordinate donor and alumni communications, campaign materials, and impact messaging.  Ensure communications align with institutional priorities and support engagement and fundraising objectives. Team Leadership:  Supervise and mentor the Advancement Services team.  Foster a collaborative, service-oriented, and solutions-focused culture.  Support professional development and continuous improvement. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required. Minimum of five years of progressively responsible experience in advancement services, development operations, donor relations, prospect research, or related advancement functions. Demonstrated experience overseeing gift processing, data management, reporting, stewardship, and advancement operations. Experience with prospect research, portfolio management, and donor analytics preferred. Experience supervising staff and managing projects across multiple functions. Strong analytical, organizational, and problem solving skills with exceptional attention to detail. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to manage confidential information with discretion and professionalism. Experience with advancement CRM systems and reporting tools. Preferred Characteristics: Strategic yet highly execution oriented. Collaborative and service-minded Comfortable balancing operational detail with broader institutional goals. Interested in helping strengthen and modernize advancement infrastructure in a growing and mission-driven environment. Committed to fostering meaningful donor and alumni relationships through strong, efficient systems and thoughtful stewardship practices. Salary Range:  $95,000 annually. 40-hour work week. Exact compensation based on candidate skills and experience.  How to Apply:  Applications accepted only via www.chatham.edu/careers  (direct link is https://chatham.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/ChathamUniversity/job/Pittsburgh-PA/Senior-Director-of-Advancement-Services_JR00000961 ) and follow the instructions to complete the application process. To ensure full consideration, please include:  Cover Letter outlining your qualifications for the position  Curriculum Vitae or Resume  Contact information for three professional references  All application materials should be uploaded at the same time at the time of application. The system will not allow applicants to make edits to their applications after submission. Chatham University strives to promote a campus environment that understands and embraces multiculturalism while increasing individuals' intercultural competence. We actively work to build and sustain a diverse and culturally vibrant campus, which promotes employee and student success and retention.   Chatham University is an Equal Opportunity Employer with a strong commitment to diversity, inclusion, and equity. Chatham University does not discriminate on the basis of race, creed, color, religion, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, age, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, marital or family status, political affiliation, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law."
    },
    "https://chatham.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/ChathamUniversity/job/Pittsburgh-PA/Assistant-Men-s-Wrestling-Coach_JR00000938": {
      "title": "Assistant Men's Wrestling Coach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-20\nPart time\n\nChatham University welcomes your interest in employment opportunities and encourages you to review open positions. Please note that Chatham does not accept unsolicited applications. Assistant Men’s Wrestling Coach Chatham University is seeking a dedicated and enthusiastic Assistant Men’s Wrestling Coach to support all aspects of its NCAA Division III Wrestling Program, a member of the Presidents' Athletic Conference (PAC). This position offers an exciting opportunity to contribute to the development of student-athletes both on and off the mat while helping advance a competitive and successful wrestling program. The Assistant Wrestling Coach will assist the Head Wrestling Coach in the daily operation and administration of the wrestling program. Responsibilities include recruiting qualified student-athletes, supporting student-athlete development, assisting with program operations, promoting compliance with NCAA and conference regulations, and representing the program at university and community events. Duties and Responsibilities: Assist in planning, organizing, implementing, and evaluating recruiting efforts to attract qualified student-athletes. Support the development, assessment, and retention of student-athletes through coaching, mentorship, and leadership development. Assist with practice planning, competition preparation, and overall program operations. Help manage program resources, equipment, and operational needs. Promote student-athlete success in academics, athletics, and personal growth. Assist in supporting campus initiatives and coordinating athletic events that enhance school spirit and community engagement. Ensure compliance with all University, NCAA Division III, and Presidents' Athletic Conference (PAC) rules, regulations, and policies. Represent the wrestling program at on-campus events, admissions programs, and University functions. Represent the wrestling program at recruiting events, tournaments, and high school competitions. Foster a positive team culture that emphasizes sportsmanship, integrity, leadership, and academic achievement. Perform other duties as assigned by the Head Wrestling Coach. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree required. Strong leadership abilities and exceptional character. Excellent communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Availability to work evenings, weekends, and holidays as required. Commitment to the mission and values of NCAA Division III athletics. Minimum of one year of collegiate coaching experience and NCAA Division III experience as a coach or student-athlete preferred. How to Apply:  Applications accepted only via www.chatham.edu/careers  (direct link is https://chatham.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/ChathamUniversity/job/Pittsburgh-PA/Assistant-Men-s-Wrestling-Coach_JR00000938 ) and follow the instructions to complete the application process. To ensure full consideration, please include:  Cover Letter outlining your qualifications for the position  Curriculum Vitae or Resume  Contact information for three professional references  All application materials should be uploaded at the same time at the time of application. The system will not allow applicants to make edits to their applications after submission. Chatham University strives to promote a campus environment that understands and embraces multiculturalism while increasing individuals' intercultural competence. We actively work to build and sustain a diverse and culturally vibrant campus, which promotes employee and student success and retention.   Chatham University is an Equal Opportunity Employer with a strong commitment to diversity, inclusion, and equity. Chatham University does not discriminate on the basis of race, creed, color, religion, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, age, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, marital or family status, political affiliation, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law."
    },
    "https://chatham.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/ChathamUniversity/job/Pittsburgh-PA/Assistant-Women-s-Wrestling-Coach_JR00000939": {
      "title": "Assistant Women's Wrestling Coach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-13\nPart time\n\nChatham University welcomes your interest in employment opportunities and encourages you to review open positions. Please note that Chatham does not accept unsolicited applications. Assistant Women’s Wrestling Coach Chatham University is seeking a dedicated and enthusiastic Assistant Women's Wrestling Coach to support all aspects of its NCAA Division III Women's Wrestling Program, a member of the Presidents' Athletic Conference (PAC). This position offers an excellent opportunity to help build a competitive program while fostering the academic, athletic, and personal development of student-athletes. The Assistant Women's Wrestling Coach will assist the Head Women's Wrestling Coach in the daily operation of the wrestling program. Responsibilities include recruiting prospective student-athletes, supporting coaching and player development, assisting with program administration, and ensuring compliance with NCAA Division III, PAC, and University regulations. The successful candidate will serve as a positive role model and ambassador for Chatham University and its athletics programs. Duties and Responsibilities: Assist in planning, organizing, implementing, and evaluating recruiting efforts to attract qualified student-athletes. Support athletic planning, program development, and the assessment of student-athlete performance, retention, personal growth, and leadership development. Assist with practice planning, competition preparation, and day-to-day program operations. Help oversee and manage program resources and equipment. Support campus initiatives and assist in coordinating athletic events that enhance campus engagement and school spirit. Ensure compliance with all Chatham University, NCAA Division III, and Presidents' Athletic Conference (PAC) rules, regulations, and policies. Represent the Women's Wrestling program at on-campus events, admissions programs, and University functions. Represent the program at recruiting events, tournaments, and high school competitions. Promote a culture of sportsmanship, integrity, academic achievement, and personal responsibility. Perform other duties as assigned by the Head Women's Wrestling Coach. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree required. Excellent leadership skills and strong character. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work evenings, weekends, and holidays as required. Commitment to the educational mission of NCAA Division III athletics. How to Apply:  Applications accepted only via www.chatham.edu/careers  (direct link is https://chatham.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/ChathamUniversity/job/Pittsburgh-PA/Assistant-Women-s-Wrestling-Coach_JR00000939 ) and follow the instructions to complete the application process. To ensure full consideration, please include:  Cover Letter outlining your qualifications for the position  Curriculum Vitae or Resume  Contact information for three professional references  All application materials should be uploaded at the same time at the time of application. The system will not allow applicants to make edits to their applications after submission. Chatham University strives to promote a campus environment that understands and embraces multiculturalism while increasing individuals' intercultural competence. We actively work to build and sustain a diverse and culturally vibrant campus, which promotes employee and student success and retention.   Chatham University is an Equal Opportunity Employer with a strong commitment to diversity, inclusion, and equity. Chatham University does not discriminate on the basis of race, creed, color, religion, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, age, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, marital or family status, political affiliation, or any other characteristic protected by app